Inferno on QEMU spike
=====================

Status: HTIF console + Dis shell smoke PASS (`./smoke.sh`).

QEMU `-M spike` HTIF requires ELF symbols `tohost` / `fromhost`.
`jl -H5` emits a loadable ELF **without section headers / symtab**.
`elf-htif-syms.py` injects a minimal `.symtab` / `.strtab` after link.

Important: QEMU maps HTIF over the whole `[min(tohost,fromhost), max+8)`
span.  Two separate BSS symbols are not kept adjacent by `jl`, so a gap
turns ordinary data into "Invalid htif".  Board `l.s` therefore allocates
one 16-byte `tohost` cell; `fromhost` is `tohost+8` (C + ELF inject).

Also drain the PUTC ack in `fromhost` — QEMU leaves `0x100|char` there,
and `clockpoll`'s getc would otherwise echo forever (CRLF flood).

Build:
	cd os/spike
	mk SYSTARG=os OBJTYPE=riscv64 SHELLTYPE=sh INIT=spikeinit install
	./smoke.sh

Run:
	qemu-system-riscv64 -M spike -nographic -bios none \
		-kernel $ROOT/Inferno/riscv64/bin/ispike
